# python-sbom

[PyPI]
[Supported Python versions]
[check]
[Documentation Status]
[Downloads]
[OpenSSF Scorecard]

Software bills of materials (SBOMs) for Python distributions. python-sbom
writes a [CycloneDX]
SBOM into every [wheel] you build,
where [PEP 770] (a Python Enhancement Proposal) tells installers to keep
it. The SBOM
records your project, the runtime dependencies it declares, any wheels it
bundles, and the build toolchain, and a
rebuild with the same inputs reproduces it byte for byte.

## Use

python-sbom works with every [build backend]. Pick the integration for
yours:

| Backend                                                                  
                                                                           
                                                            | Add to
`[build-system] requires` | Turn it on                                     
                                  |
|
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
| -------------------------------- |
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
|
| [hatchling]                                                              
                                                                           
                             | `python-sbom[hatch]`             |
`[tool.hatch.build.hooks.python-sbom]`                                     
      |
| [pdm-backend]                                                            
                                                                           
                          | `python-sbom[pdm]`               |
`[tool.python-sbom]`                                                       
      |
| [setuptools]                                                             
                                                                           
                               | `python-sbom[setuptools]`        |
`[tool.python-sbom]`                                                       
      |
| any other, such as [meson-python], [maturin], [scikit-build-core] or
[flit-core] | `python-sbom`                    | `build-backend =
"python_sbom.backend"`, and your backend in `[tool.python-sbom]` |

With hatchling:

```toml
[build-system]
build-backend = "hatchling.build"
requires = ["hatchling>=1.28", "python-sbom[hatch]>=0.2"]

[tool.hatch.build.hooks.python-sbom]
```

With meson-python, or any backend without a plugin, python-sbom wraps it:

```toml
[build-system]
build-backend = "python_sbom.backend"
requires = ["meson-python>=0.18", "python-sbom>=0.2"]

[tool.python-sbom]
build-backend = "mesonpy"
```

For a wheel built outside the build interface, such as with [`maturin
build`], or renamed after
it by [`auditwheel repair`], embed the SBOM afterwards:

```console
python-sbom embed dist/*.whl
```

To convert and validate SBOMs in continuous integration (CI), install the
command line in a tool environment of its own
with [pipx] or [uv]:

```console
pipx install 'python-sbom[validate]'
python-sbom validate dist/
```

